  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Background
    
    A Nightshelf mystic, thief, and former member of The Communion — the deep-ice cult whose blood-rites commune with presences beneath The Berg. ☽'Iarlocias was born during the Clever Ice Age and trained under Zhachelang, a Communion elder, where she was regarded as one of the cult's most capable practitioners. Her known disciplines include Fissure☽ Aurora, ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral, Shawl☽ Sun, ☽Silv-glaciere☽ Arts, Star∴eternal, and Veil∴numb — an unusually broad range that speaks either to exceptional aptitude or to the Communion's willingness to invest heavily in students it intended to keep.
    
    She carries frost-scars on her flippers that she has never explained. I note this without further comment.
    
    ## The Break
    
    ☽'Iarlocias stole the Thaw-Paths Medallion — an aurora-glass artifact of considerable and poorly understood power — from the Communion's inner shrine. Her stated reason, relayed through intermediaries rather than direct testimony, was that the cult's blood-rites were waking something beneath the ice, or the Medallion was using the rites to wake itself, and she could no longer distinguish between these possibilities. The distinction may matter less than she believed.
    
    She also recovered the ☽'micseleia' Dagger, a shadow-steel blade housing a captured fire-core, from the orca war-leader Thung Thrakrek by theft. The Nightshelf Deep-Archive register notes the Dagger bears an irreparable fracture that widens with each use — damage sustained during an Incursion that four skilled practitioners have failed to reverse.
    
    She then descended into ☽'shadow Umbrsulcavus~, the shadow-spaces near The Forgotten Shore where The Berg preserves memories the Nightshelf buried. The accounts agree that something there recognized what she carried and attended to her with focused regard. What she found ended her faith in Communion teachings. She has never stated what it was directly — only in warnings that read as proverbs until they prove prophetic.
    
    ## The Medallion's Disposition
    
    ☽'Iarlocias wrapped the Thaw-Paths Medallion in ceremonial thread and abandoned it in the third cavern of ☽'secret Sanctninicaesis~, deliberately suppressing its radiance. When the lector ☽'Ilsancuia Depth-walker later discovered and restored it, ☽'Iarlocias warned that every restoration of the Medallion's brightness invites the deep to reach upward. ☽'Ilsancuia did not heed this. ☽'Ilsancuia is dead.
    
    ## The Accord
    
    ☽'Iarlocias witnessed the signing of the Accord of Still Pools and Frost Zenith — a treaty between Aureate and the ☽'shadow Covens' Order ratified at The Frost Zenith. She is listed as unaffiliated. Her testimony on deep-tunnel conditions shaped the accord's provisions on tunnel access restrictions and corruption sanctification. She did not sign. She left before the ink set.
    
    ## Present Status
    
    ☽'Iarlocias moves through The Berg's lower caverns with deliberate silence — no wasted motion, heavy charcoal wraps concealing a fire-core amulet she no longer wears. Her left flipper twitches in a repeating pattern: three taps, pause, two taps. The tic began after ☽'shadow Umbrsulcavus~ and has not stopped. She adheres to the Firekeeper∴Doctrine and operates under the Dawn Mandate's provisions, though the relationship between these affiliations and her Communion apostasy remains unclear from available sources.
    
    She speaks in fragments and silences. Those who knew her before say she still smiles — but only as someone who has already chosen and is waiting for the ice to confirm it.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771581797778_0", anchor: "I note this without further comment.", text: "The reader will observe that I extended to ☽'Iarlocias a courtesy I have never been extended myself. The Nightshelf sent a formal apology for mine. I have not opened it. These two facts are not related to the entry. They are not unrelated to it either.", type: :tangent, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771581797778_1", anchor: "the Communion's willingness to invest heavily in students it intended to keep", text: "The Communion does not invest in students it intends to keep. It invests in students it intends to use. The distinction is the entire architecture of her break.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771581797778_2", anchor: "☽'Ilsancuia is dead.", text: "I let this stand as two sentences and a full stop, and the implication is causal: she warned, the warning went unheeded, the subject died. But the Deep-Archive register attributes ☽'Ilsancuia's death to tunnel collapse during routine survey — corruption-adjacent, not demonstrably medallion-related. I wrote a sequence that reads as consequence. The record does not support the weight I gave it. It may deserve the weight anyway.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771581797778_3", anchor: "three taps, pause, two taps", text: "Someone counted. She moves through lower caverns alone. Either this was observed at the Accord signing — the only documented gathering where she was visible to unaffiliated witnesses — or someone followed her afterward. Given what she carries, the second possibility is not comforting.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
